\pard\sa100 EasyTube is a \b free and open-source\b0  app, created with the help of \b Claude Code\b0 , Anthropic\'92s coding assistant.\par
\pard\sb160\sa60\b\fs24 Why EasyTube exists\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100 EasyTube is built entirely on \b yt-dlp\b0 , a very powerful and widely trusted open-source project maintained by a community of developers and contributors. But yt-dlp has no interface: it only runs from the command line, which is complicated for most people.\par
\pard\sa100 EasyTube simply gives it a modern, all-in-one graphical interface: you paste a link, see the preview, choose the quality and the folder, and you\'92re off. yt-dlp and FFmpeg are already included, so there is nothing else to install.\par
\pard\sb160\sa60\b\fs24 A big thank you to yt-dlp\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100 Thanks to the developers and contributors of yt-dlp, and to those of FFmpeg, for their remarkable work: without them, EasyTube wouldn\'92t exist.\par
\pard\sb160\sa60\b\fs24 Free software, and its licenses\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100 EasyTube\'92s own code is released under the \b MIT License\b0 : you may use, copy, change and share it freely. The programs and the font included keep their own licenses: \b yt-dlp\b0  (Unlicense; GPL-3.0 or later for the .exe build), \b FFmpeg\b0  (GPL-3.0), \b Electron\b0  (MIT) and the \b Bricolage Grotesque\b0  font (SIL Open Font License). The full texts, with links to the source code, are installed in the \b licenses\b0  folder next to the program, and in Settings > About.\par
\pard\sb160\sa60\b\fs24 Good to know\b0\fs20\par
\pard\sa100 EasyTube is an independent project, not affiliated with yt-dlp nor endorsed by its authors. It is designed for personal use: please respect copyright and the terms of use of the sites you use.\par
